meta {
  name: Get a guest token
  type: http
  seq: 1
  tags: [
    Customer_Auth
  ]
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v2/customer-auth/guest
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.timestamp: isDefined
  res.body.error: isDefined
  res.body.data: isDefined
  res.body.meta: isDefined
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 200 && res.body.data && res.body.data.token) {
    bru.setVar("guestToken", res.body.data.token);
  }
}

docs {
  A token for a customer without an account (an app before sign-in): in `X-Customer-Auth-Token` it opens the cart, checkout, addresses and orders (`customer-cart/*`, `customer-account/address/*`, `customer-order/create`, `list`, `show`); the profile, password and order cancel give 403 `customer-token-required` — the guest signs in to cancel. A guest places an order without signing in: the order lives on a hidden guest account tied to this token only, never to an existing customer with the same phone or email, and the guest sees it while the token lives. No order emails are sent to a guest; SMS goes to the phone of the delivery address. The token lives 90 days; renew it before with `guest_token`, the new token keeps the cart and orders. When the guest signs in or up with `guest_token` (`customer-auth/sign-in` by email and password, or `customer-auth/confirm`), the cart, orders and addresses move to the customer and the guest token stops working. With an app key, one IP may start checkout for 20 new guests and place 10 guest orders an hour (429).
}
